\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

Schema-induced degradation in training-free LLM extraction operates through two channels (count-driven recall decline, confusability-driven type confusion) with bounded interaction in RE (TOST $p = 0.003$ at $\pm 3$\,pp) but coupling in NER. Channel~1 replicates across scales; Channel~2 attenuates on smaller models. BCS enables pre-hoc schema screening.

